From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:33:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] CP decode: the remote head groups as one attention call
 behind G6_CP_ONECHAIN=1

Past R each rank runs the other ranks' head groups over its own keys: today one k_vget, cp_group (scores, cp_softmax,
context parts, merge) and k_vput per group, 18 launches a layer at TP=4. With G6_CP_ONECHAIN=1 one k_vget_heads puts
the three groups' q / rope side by side and g6_attn_cp_groups runs one 48-head call whose merge (merge_parts_g) writes
each group's partial into its own block; the three puts follow in the S1 order (8 launches). Every kernel indexes a
(row, head) by row * heads + h and batches heads in groups that divide 16, so each head runs the 16-head kernel on the
same operands in the same order: the published partials are byte-identical (engine/attn/tests/cpgroups.cu compares
them and times both forms on one GPU). TP=4 only and not with G6_ATTN_FLIP (the boot dies otherwise); about 1.3 MB per
CP fabric row for the gathered queries and the call's own scratch. Off (default): unchanged.
